<!--
  ============================================================================
  Flamebow_TagWiden.xml                     Jawa_Armoury · authored 2026-08-22
  ============================================================================

  Owner's instruction, 2026-08-22 01:05:
    "We should put tags on the flame bows so that more people can use them too,
     like the deep tribes especially."

  WHY A PATCH IS NEEDED AT ALL, AND WHY IT ALONE WAS NOT ENOUGH
  =============================================================
  `ThingDef/Flamebow` was on the Cherry Picker kill list. Cherry Picker does not
  delete a cut def - it NEUTERS it, and part of neutering a weapon is emptying
  `weaponTags`. So every tag added here would have been wiped at load and the
  patch would have looked like it silently failed.

  ⇒ The owner removed `ThingDef/Flamebow` from the kill list on 2026-08-22 01:12
  (1347 -> 1346 entries; backup `.bak-20260822-flamebow`, repo mirror synced).
  THAT step is a precondition for this file. If the flamebow is ever re-cut,
  this patch stops working and logs nothing.

  WHAT BIOTECH ALREADY SHIPS - read from the source, not assumed
  ==============================================================
    C:\Program Files (x86)\Steam\steamapps\common\RimWorld\Data\Biotech\
      Defs\ThingDefs_Misc\Weapons\RangedIndustrial.xml:185-197
        <MarketValue>45</MarketValue>
        <weaponTags>
          <li>NeolithicRangedFlame</li>
        </weaponTags>

  ⇒ Un-cutting alone already repairs `Tribal_Archer_Fire`, whose only tag is
  `NeolithicRangedFlame` and whose budget is 80. That tag had ZERO usable
  carriers while the flamebow was cut, which is why the kind spawned 0/5 armed
  when measured live on 2026-08-21
  (`infrastructure/state/observed/2026-08-21/armed_sweep_48/`).

  WHAT THIS FILE ADDS, AND THE ARITHMETIC BEHIND EACH TAG
  ========================================================
  Measured budgets and tags, from the 2026-08-21 def dump:

    Tribal_Archer        money  80- 80   tags [NeolithicRangedBasic]
    Tribal_Hunter        money 100-100   tags [NeolithicRangedDecent]
    Tribal_HeavyArcher   money 250-250   tags [NeolithicRangedHeavy]
    Tribal_Archer_Fire   money  80- 80   tags [NeolithicRangedFlame]      <- already fixed

  The flamebow costs 45, so it is affordable to Archer (80) and Hunter (100)
  with room to spare. Adding those two tags is what lets the Deep Desert Tribes
  actually field it: `TribeCivil` fields `Tribal_Archer`, `Tribal_HeavyArcher`
  and `Tribal_Hunter`, and NONE of its group makers name a fire kind.

  ⛔ `NeolithicRangedHeavy` is deliberately NOT added. A 45-silver light bow has
  no business in a 250-budget heavy slot; it would make the HeavyArcher strictly
  cheaper and remove the distinction between the two archer tiers.

  WHY THIS MATTERS BEYOND ONE KIND - the bow palette is nearly gone
  =================================================================
  Measured 2026-08-22 against the dump and the kill list: of the primitive-ranged
  cluster, **2 usable and 12 cut**. `NeolithicRangedBasic` has 5 carriers left,
  `NeolithicRangedDecent` 6, `NeolithicRangedAdvanced` 3. Live spawns of
  `TribeCivil`'s archers on 2026-08-21 drew nerve spikers, throwing knives, a
  fungal spore and throwspikes - and 6 of 18 drew nothing at all. NOT ONE BOW.
  This patch puts an actual bow back in the tribal pool.

  🔴 A CONSEQUENCE THE OWNER SHOULD SEE BEFORE THIS SHIPS
  ========================================================
  This makes incendiary arrows available to EVERY `Tribal_Archer` and
  `Tribal_Hunter` in the game, not only the Deep Desert Tribes - those are
  vanilla kinds fielded by many tribal factions.

  ⚠️ And `PLANT_GROWTH_SPEC.md` multiplies every plant's GrowthRate, while
  `hydrology_and_fire_ecology.md` R-H3 makes that growth the fuel for a savanna
  that burns forever. Fire arrows in the hands of every tribal archer on a world
  built to burn is a LOUD change. It may be exactly the drama wanted; it is not
  a quiet one. If it proves too much, the cheap dial is to drop
  `NeolithicRangedBasic` here and leave only `NeolithicRangedDecent`, halving the
  number of kinds that can draw it.

  SAFETY
  ======
  Wrapped in a conditional on the def existing, so if Biotech is ever inactive
  the file is a silent no-op rather than a wall of red. `PatchOperationAdd` onto
  the existing `weaponTags` node APPENDS; it does not replace, so
  `NeolithicRangedFlame` survives.
  ============================================================================
-->
<Patch>

  <Operation Class="PatchOperationConditional">
    <xpath>/Defs/ThingDef[defName="Flamebow"]/weaponTags</xpath>
    <match Class="PatchOperationAdd">
      <xpath>/Defs/ThingDef[defName="Flamebow"]/weaponTags</xpath>
      <value>
        <li>NeolithicRangedBasic</li>
        <li>NeolithicRangedDecent</li>
      </value>
    </match>
  </Operation>

</Patch>
